 "evidence": {
  "実例": [
   {
    "quote": "例えば、最新鋭設備の導入により省力化を図った場合、従業員数が減った分だけ労働生産性が上がります",
    "url": "https://note.com/yajirushi_works/n/nacbfd931b027",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "限界利益は、企業の内部分析でも使われ、例えば、部門毎や商品毎、地域毎など、それぞれに限界利益率を求めることで簡単に利益分析（収益性の明確化）をすることができ、改善すべき点を洗い出すのに便利です",
    "url": "https://note.com/yajirushi_works/n/nacbfd931b027",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "A common metric by which SaaS companies track their performance is annual recurring revenue (ARR) per employee. As was the case with the last post, the data and analysis below on ARR per employee comes from our 15th annual survey of more than 1,000 SaaS companies, which was completed in March.",
    "url": "https://www.saas-capital.com/blog-posts/revenue-per-employee-benchmarks-for-private-saas-companies/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "The chart below shows the median ARR per employee broken down by company size. For example, the chart shows that companies with $1 million to $3 million in ARR have a median ARR per employee of $109,644.",
    "url": "https://www.saas-capital.com/blog-posts/revenue-per-employee-benchmarks-for-private-saas-companies/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "The chart below shows the median ARR per employee broken down by company size and funding type, equity-backed or bootstrapped. For example, equity-backed companies with $5 million to $10 million in ARR have a median ARR per employee of $152,295. Meanwhile, bootstrapped companies of the same size show a median ARR per full-time equivalent (FTE) of $177,240.",
    "url": "https://www.saas-capital.com/blog-posts/revenue-per-employee-benchmarks-for-private-saas-companies/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "For example, if a company earns $100,000 in revenue and has 10 full-time people, the RPE would be $10,000.",
    "url": "https://www.hibob.com/financial-metrics/revenue-per-employee/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "For example, a sudden increase in RPE might look positive on the surface. But if the change stems from layoffs or high turnover, the story is very different. By digging into the “why” behind your RPE numbers, you can set thoughtful targets that evolve as your company grows.",
    "url": "https://www.hibob.com/financial-metrics/revenue-per-employee/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "For example, if a company generates $1 million in total revenue during 2022 and has 100 full-time people, the",
    "url": "https://www.hibob.com/financial-metrics/revenue-per-employee/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "For example:",
    "url": "https://www.hibob.com/financial-metrics/revenue-per-employee/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Worked Example",
    "url": "https://www.hrbench.com/resource/learn/revenue-per-employee",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "When RPE is falling, two root causes explain most cases. Headcount grew faster than revenue, meaning the organization hired ahead of actual demand. Or revenue declined while headcount held steady, meaning a retention or hiring freeze decision is already overdue. Each cause calls for a different response.",
    "url": "https://www.hrbench.com/resource/learn/revenue-per-employee",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Example:",
    "url": "https://www.hrbench.com/resource/learn/revenue-per-employee",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "For example, a software company pulling in $1.76 million per employee and a hospital averaging $8,700 are both running normal operations for their industry. One runs on code and licensing. The other runs on a large network of staff and overnight shifts. We may be looking at the same metric, but each has a completely different story.",
    "url": "https://www.venasolutions.com/blog/average-revenue-per-employee",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Labor-intensive industries such as restaurants, general retail and hospitals cluster at the low end, with RPE figures below $35,000 in some cases, reflecting high headcount relative to revenue.",
    "url": "https://www.venasolutions.com/blog/average-revenue-per-employee",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "For example, a software company and a hospital can both be healthy, well-run businesses and show wildly different RPE figures. The U.S. total market average sits at $111,000 per employee, but that number masks enormous variation by industry.",
    "url": "https://www.venasolutions.com/blog/average-revenue-per-employee",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Cross-industry comparisons also have limits. An industry’s structure shapes RPE as much as management quality does, which is why our previous example of comparing a hospital to a software company on this metric tells you very little of analytical value.",
    "url": "https://www.venasolutions.com/blog/average-revenue-per-employee",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
